NNAAMMEE
     mmeennuu..lluuaa — bootloader dynamic menu module

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     mmeennuu..lluuaa contains the main functionality required to build a dynamic menu
     system.  It also contains definitions for the built-in menus, some of
     which are influenced by loader(8) environment variables.

     Before hooking into the functionality provided by mmeennuu..lluuaa, it must be
     included with a statement such as the following:

           local menu = require("menu")

   MMEENNUU DDEEFFIINNIITTIIOONNSS
     Menus are represented in mmeennuu..lluuaa as a table.  That table mmuusstt contain an
     _e_n_t_r_i_e_s key.

     If the value of the _e_n_t_r_i_e_s key is itself a table, then each value in
     this table defines a single entry in this menu.  See _M_E_N_U _I_T_E_M
     _D_E_F_I_N_I_T_I_O_N_S for the structure of each entry.

     _e_n_t_r_i_e_s may also be a function.  This function must return a table, each
     value of which defines a single entry in this menu.  See _M_E_N_U _I_T_E_M
     _D_E_F_I_N_I_T_I_O_N_S.

   MMEENNUU IITTEEMM DDEEFFIINNIITTIIOONNSS
     The following keys may be defined for a menu item:

           eennttrryy__ttyyppee             The type of this menu entry.  See _M_E_N_U _I_T_E_M
                                  _T_Y_P_E_S.

           ccaarroouusseell__iidd            A unique string id for this carousel.  A
                                  carousel is a menu entry that rotates
                                  through a selection of items.  Used for
                                  storage of the carousel's current setting.

           vviissiibbllee                A lambda that returns true if this menu item
                                  should be visible and false if it should not
                                  be visible.

           iitteemmss                  A table (or a lambda that returns a table)
                                  of the possible choices for this carousel.

           nnaammee                   A string (or a lambda that returns a string)
                                  containing the current name of this item.

           ffuunncc                   The function executed when this entry is se‐
                                  lected.  Every type except for
                                  ccoorree..MMEENNUU__SSEEPPAARRAATTOORR may have a ffuunncc.

           ssuubbmmeennuu                The submenu menu definition to draw when
                                  this entry is selected.

           aalliiaass                  A table of case-sensitive aliases for this
                                  menu entry.  All menu entries that can be
                                  selected may have any number of aalliiaass en‐
                                  tries.

     eennttrryy__ttyyppee is the only required key for every entry type.  nnaammee is re‐
     quired for all entry types except for ccoorree..MMEENNUU__SSEEPPAARRAATTOORR.

   MMEENNUU IITTEEMM TTYYPPEESS
     The menu item type constants are defined in core.lua(8).  The following
     types are available:

           ccoorree..MMEENNUU__RREETTUURRNN          Return to the parent menu.  If the cur‐
                                     rent menu is the default menu, mmeennuu..lluuaa
                                     will exit the menu and begin the autoboot
                                     sequence (if applicable).  This type of
                                     menu entry may execute ffuunncc, when se‐
                                     lected, and has a nnaammee.

           ccoorree..MMEENNUU__EENNTTRRYY           A normal menu entry that executes ffuunncc
                                     when selected, and has a nnaammee.

           ccoorree..MMEENNUU__SSEEPPAARRAATTOORR       A menu entry that serves as a separator.
                                     It may have a nnaammee.

           ccoorree..MMEENNUU__SSUUBBMMEENNUU         A menu entry that opens ssuubbmmeennuu when se‐
                                     lected.  It may have a nnaammee.

           ccoorree..MMEENNUU__CCAARROOUUSSEELL__EENNTTRRYY  A menu entry that rotates through iitteemmss
                                     like a carousel.  ffuunncc is executed when
                                     selected, and the callback is passed the
                                     choice index, name of the current choice,
                                     and the table of choices.

   EEXXPPOORRTTEEDD MMEENNUUSS
     The following menus are exported by mmeennuu..lluuaa:

           mmeennuu..ddeeffaauulltt            The default menu to draw.  Set to
                                   mmeennuu..wweellccoommee by default.

           mmeennuu..wweellccoommee            The welcome menu.  Contains single and
                                   multi user boot options, as well as entries
                                   to access other menus.

           mmeennuu..bboooott__ooppttiioonnss       The "Boot Options" menu.

           mmeennuu..bboooott__eennvviirroonnmmeennttss  The "Boot Environments" menu.  This menu is
                                   only visible if the system is booted on a
                                   ZFS partition and more than one boot envi‐
                                   ronment was detected at boot.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     To replace the default boot menu with a simple boot menu:

           local core = require("core")
           local menu = require("menu")

           menu.default = {
                   entries = {
                           {
                                   entry_type = core.MENU_ENTRY,
                                   name = "Boot",
                                   func = core.boot,
                           },
                           {
                                   entry_type = core.MENU_CAROUSEL_ENTRY,
                                   carousel_id = "unique_boot_entry_name",
                                   items = {"NO", "YES"},
                                   name = function(_, choice, _)
                                           return "Option: " .. choice
                                   end,
                                   func = function(_, _, _)
                                           loader.setenv("some_envvar", "some_value")
                                   end,
                           },
                   },
           }

     To add another option to the welcome menu:

           local core = require("core")
           local menu = require("menu")

           local my_entry = {
                   entry_type = core.MENU_ENTRY,
                   name = "Fancy Boot",
                   func = core.boot,
           },

           local stock_entries = menu.welcome.entries
           function menu.welcome.entries()
                   local ents = stock_entries()
                   ents[#ents + 1] = my_entry
                   return ents
           end

     To create a vendor submenu or other vendor menu option, override
     mmeennuu..wweellccoommee..aallll__eennttiirreess..vveennddoorr like so:

           local core = require("core")
           local menu = require("menu")

           -- Fill in with vendor specific entries
           local vendor_options = {
                   entries = {
                   ...
                   },
           }

           local welcome_entries = menu.welcome.all_entries
           welcome_entries.vendor = {
                   entry_type = core.MENU_SUBMENU,
                   name = color.highlight("V") .. "endor Options",
                   submenu = vendor_options,
                   alias = {"v", "V"},
                   visible = function()
                           return true
                   end,
           }
     In the above example, vveennddoorr__ooppttiioonnss is a local variable that defines the
     vendor submenu.

     To add an additional option, change the mmeennuu..bboooott__ooppttiioonnss..eennttrriieess array.
     The following illustrates this concept:

           -- This is a silly example that rotates local_option through the values
           -- 0 to 4.  local_option would still need to be used elsewhere.
           local local_option = 0

           -- The `entries` of a menu may either be a table or a function.  In this
           -- example we're augmenting a menu that just has a static table, but if we
           -- wanted to be more robust then we would need to instead check the type
           -- of `stock_options` here to determine our next move.
           --
           -- If `entries` is a table, then the stock menu system won't be changing it
           -- so we can just add our menu option as we do below.
           --
           -- If `entries` is a function, then we would need to provide a new function to
           -- replace `entries` that does a core.deepCopyTable() of the result and adds
           -- the below item to it.  The deep copy is necessary to avoid duplicating our
           -- new menu item and allowing the menu to alter its behavior however it pleases.
           local stock_options = menu.boot_options.entries
           stock_options[#stock_options + 1] = {
                   entry_type = core.MENU_ENTRY,
                   name = function()
                           return color.highlight('L') ..
                               "ocal Option     : " .. local_option
                   end,
                   func = function()
                           local_option = (local_option + 1) % 5
                   end,
                   alias= {"l", "L"}
           }

